        <mxCell id="records" value="Intranet records returned&#xa;&#xa;api.example.com      → 10.254.28.115&#xa;api-dev.example.com  → 10.254.21.159" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=10;align=left;spacingLeft=10;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1265" y="395" width="270" height="90" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="blackhole" value="✕&#xa;silent drop&#xa;no ICMP&#xa;→ client timeout" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;dashed=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1265" y="545" width="150" height="80" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-ec2-res" value="1  dig @172.17.0.2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;fontSize=9;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#b85450;fontColor=#b85450;" parent="1" source="ec2" target="resolver2" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-res-ram" value="2  rule match → forward" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;fontSize=9;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#b85450;fontColor=#b85450;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;" parent="1" source="resolver2" target="ram" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-ram-ep" value="3  Resolver-internal hop&#xa;NO VPC peering / TGW&#xa;required for this leg" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;fontSize=9;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#82b366;fontColor=#82b366;fontStyle=1;" parent="1" source="inbound-q" target="outbound-ep" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-enia-dns" value="4a  UDP/TCP 53  ✓" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;fontSize=9;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#82b366;fontColor=#82b366;" parent="1" source="eni-a" target="dns-onprem" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-enib-bh" value="4b  suspected blackhole" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;fontSize=9;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#b85450;fontColor=#b85450;dashed=1;" parent="1" source="eni-b" target="blackhole" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-ctrl-1" value="CONTROL TEST A&#xa;dig @10.4.44.80 → works&#xa;(does NOT exercise the shared rules)" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;fontSize=9;dashed=1;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#996f00;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=0.25;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.15;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" parent="1" source="ec2" target="eni-a" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <Array as="points">
              <mxPoint x="540" y="80" />
              <mxPoint x="620" y="80" />
              <mxPoint x="620" y="441" />
            </Array>
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e-ctrl-2" value="CONTROL TEST B — dig @185.46.212.88 → works" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;fontSize=9;dashed=1;strokeColor=#82b366;fontColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=2;exitX=0.5;exitY=0;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" parent="1" source="ec2" target="dns-onprem" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <Array as="points">
              <mxPoint x="255" y="90" />
              <mxPoint x="1400" y="90" />
            </Array>
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note-timeout" value="WHAT THE TIMEOUT PROVES  —  read this first&#xa;&#xa;Rule-matched names time out, but every other name resolves&#xa;through the SAME 172.17.0.2. Therefore the shared rule IS&#xa;matching in the consumer VPC — if it were not, the query would&#xa;fall through to recursive resolution and return SOMETHING&#xa;(a public answer, NXDOMAIN, or SERVFAIL). Silence means the&#xa;query was matched, forwarded, and no response ever came back.&#xa;&#xa;This eliminates: broken RAM share, unprogrammed association,&#xa;stale rule IDs from the CDK churn, and propagation delay.&#xa;The fault is DOWNSTREAM of the match." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=9;align=left;spacingLeft=8;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="495" width="430" height="185" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note-ttl" value="PROPAGATION / NEGATIVE-CACHE TTL — not the cause&#xa;&#xa;· Association is effective once status is COMPLETE.&#xa;  There is no documented propagation TTL to wait out.&#xa;· Negative caching applies to NXDOMAIN / NODATA, keyed to&#xa;  the authoritative SOA minimum. A TIMEOUT is not a response,&#xa;  so there is nothing to cache and nothing to expire.&#xa;· Owner deploy 12:25Z → retest 13:08Z = 43 min elapsed.&#xa;  Far beyond any plausible window. Stop waiting, start testing." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=9;align=left;spacingLeft=8;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="695" width="430" height="145" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note-qlog" value="QUERY LOGGING — expected behaviour, not a symptom&#xa;&#xa;Resolver query logging is configured PER VPC and records the&#xa;queries that ORIGINATE in that VPC.&#xa;&#xa;A query born in the consumer VPC and forwarded via the shared&#xa;rule still originates in the CONSUMER VPC. The owner VPC log&#xa;will never show it — the outbound endpoint is only the egress&#xa;vehicle, not the query origin.&#xa;&#xa;→ ACTION: enable query logging on vpc-008f2ca06864f9fca.&#xa;   Resolver logs carry rcode and answers, which separates&#xa;   &quot;never forwarded&quot; from &quot;forwarded, no reply&quot; — precisely&#xa;   the branch the timeout left open." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=9;align=left;spacingLeft=8;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="495" y="670" width="440" height="215" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note-hyp" value="HYPOTHESES — ordered by probability × cost to check&#xa;&#xa;H1  AZ asymmetry on the outbound endpoint subnets&#xa;    Two ENIs, forwarded queries are spread across both.&#xa;    Only 10.4.44.80 was ever tested. If AZ-B has no route&#xa;    to on-prem, queries landing there blackhole.&#xa;    → dig api.example.com @10.4.59.249     ONE COMMAND&#xa;&#xa;H2  NACL on the endpoint subnets&#xa;    NACLs are stateless. Query egresses from an ephemeral&#xa;    port; if inbound UDP 1024-65535 is not allowed, the&#xa;    REPLY is dropped silently. Textbook timeout.&#xa;&#xa;H3  Rule TargetIps are not what they assume&#xa;    Never verified. An overwriting CDK deploy could have&#xa;    left them pointing at the endpoint&#39;s own IPs — a loop&#xa;    against something that does not answer queries.&#xa;    → aws route53resolver get-resolver-rule --resolver-rule-id ...&#xa;&#xa;H4  Data-plane state after control-plane churn&#xa;    Stack/rules/share recreated repeatedly 11:35Z-12:25Z with&#xa;    two deploys racing. Control plane can report COMPLETE&#xa;    while the data plane holds an older generation.&#xa;    → legitimate escalation path, but LAST. Lead with H4 and&#xa;      H1-H3 come straight back in the next reply." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;fontSize=9;align=left;spacingLeft=8;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="960" y="670" width="610" height="330" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note-reqs" value="SHARED-RULE REQUIREMENTS&#xa;&#xa;· Only the RULE is shared. Endpoints cannot be shared.&#xa;· Only the CONSUMER may associate the rule with its own VPC.&#xa;· Consumer VPC needs enableDnsSupport and must use the .2 resolver.&#xa;· Consumer VPC does NOT need routing to the endpoint VPC.&#xa;  ← the usual misdiagnosis: teams debug peering/TGW here for nothing&#xa;· The ENDPOINT VPC does need routing to the rule TargetIps.&#xa;  ← this is where the real network fault lives&#xa;· One rule per domain per VPC; overlaps resolve most-specific-first.&#xa;· Rule, endpoint and VPC must be in the same Region." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontSize=9;align=left;spacingLeft=8;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1160" y="90" width="410" height="145" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note-generic" value="Domain names generalised (api.example.com / code.example.com). Resource and account IDs are as reported." style="text;html=1;fontSize=9;fontStyle=2;align=left;fontColor=#999999;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1010" width="700" height="20" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="2" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;fontSize=9;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#82b366;fontColor=#82b366;fontStyle=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="ram" target="inbound-q">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="605" y="220" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="890" y="375" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="inbound-q" value="Inbound endpoint — EXISTS?&#xa;A direct dig to 10.4.44.80 returned an answer.&#xa;An OUTBOUND endpoint does not answer queries,&#xa;so either an inbound endpoint is present and&#xa;undeclared, or the control test is invalid." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=9;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="705" y="285" width="410" height="75" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
